# Secure Cloud-Native Application Deployment on AWS EKS

## Project Overview

This project deploys and secures a simplified cloud-native application on AWS using Amazon EKS. The focus is on security controls rather than complex application development.

## Architecture

- Frontend: nginx exposed using LoadBalancer
- Backend: nginx exposed internally using ClusterIP
- Kubernetes Secret: stores dummy database credentials
- RBAC: restricts student-user permissions
- NetworkPolicy: intended to restrict backend access
- CloudWatch: enabled for EKS logging

## Tools Used

- AWS EKS
- eksctl
- kubectl
- AWS CloudShell
- Kubernetes YAML manifests
- CloudWatch

## Files

- cluster.yaml
- app.yaml
- network-policy.yaml
- deny-all.yaml
- rbac.yaml
- least-privilege-policy.json
- commands.txt

## Deployment Steps

```bash
eksctl create cluster -f cluster.yaml
kubectl apply -f app.yaml
kubectl get all -n secure-demo